.TH QFW-RUNTIME.YAML 5 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw File Formats"
.SH NAME
qfw-runtime.yaml \- select QFw resolver and local service behavior
.SH DESCRIPTION
The runtime configuration selects QPM discovery scopes and describes
components that QFw may launch. It is YAML with
.B resolver
and optional
.B local-services
mappings.
.PP
When
.B local-services
is present,
.BR qfw-setup (1)
orchestrates the requested application-owned components through the
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1)
and
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1)
lifecycle engines. The generated connection record and manager run directories
are stored in application runtime state and are released by
.BR qfw-teardown (1).
.PP
A command may select this file with
.BR --runtime-config ,
.BR QFW_RUNTIME_CONFIG ,
or an installed profile.
.PP
The installed default runtime is site-only. The installed
.B local
and
.B hybrid
profiles contain
.BR local-services .
Backend-aware example wrappers select one service from the local profile with
.BR "qfw-setup --service-id" ;
applications do not need to generate another runtime file.
.SH RESOLVER MAPPING
.TP
.B scope-order
Ordered list of QPM discovery scopes. Supported values are
.BR direct ,
.BR site ,
and
.BR local .
The value
.B local
is normalized to the allocation-local scope.
.SH LOCAL-SERVICES MAPPING
.TP
.B start-prte
Start a PRTE DVM when true.
.TP
.B start-dirsvc
Start a DEFw directory service when true.
.TP
.B start-qpm
Start the selected QPM services when true.
.TP
.B services
Service names selected from the referenced manifest. A string selects one
service. A YAML sequence selects several services.
.TP
.B service-manifest
Path to the application-scope service manifest. The installed default is
.IR prefix/share/qfw/config/services/local-services.yaml .
.TP
.B service-listen-port-base
First automatically assigned QPM listen port.
.TP
.B service-telnet-port-base
First automatically assigned QPM telnet port.
.TP
.B service-port-stride
Spacing between automatically assigned ports for multiple QPMs.
.TP
.B dirsvc
Directory launch settings. Common keys are
.BR name ,
.BR bind-host ,
.BR port ,
and
.BR telnet-port .
The value
.B auto
selects an available port during a live application-scope launch.
.TP
.B prte
PRTE launch settings. A
.B hosts
value supplies an explicit DVM host list.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
resolver:
  scope-order:
    - site

local-services:
  start-prte: false
  start-dirsvc: true
  start-qpm: true
  services:
    - fake-iqm
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1),
